  "guidance": [
    [
      "How to Use the Muscat 2027 Hybrid Plan"
    ],
    [],
    [
      "Rule",
      "Guidance",
      "Why it matters"
    ],
    [
      "Weekly structure",
      "Sun upper A; Mon rest; Tue easy run; Wed upper B + light legs/core; Thu controlled run; Fri rest; Sat long run. Every day remains visible in the tracker. Race week is the one exception: Friday is the fixed race day, so Friday is not a rest day that week.",
      "Five training days keeps two strength sessions while protecting the long run."
    ],
    [
      "Easy means easy",
      "You should usually be able to speak a full sentence. Walk before you become breathless.",
      "Your first priority is aerobic consistency, not pace."
    ],
    [
      "Strength compromise",
      "Keep upper-body work, but reduce redundant exercises and avoid failure. Lower-body lifting stays moderate and drops further in peak running weeks.",
      "Preserves strength without letting gym fatigue sabotage running."
    ],
    [
      "Progression",
      "Do not advance a long run if the prior week felt unmanageable or caused pain that altered your gait. Repeat/cut back instead.",
      "The plan is a framework, not a command to force mileage."
    ],
    [
      "Missed sessions",
      "Never cram missed mileage. Protect the long run and one easy run first; strength can be shortened.",
      "Reduces sudden load spikes."
    ],
    [
      "Peak distance",
      "Peak long run is 18 km in Week 22. The first full 21.1 km is race day.",
      "Enough endurance exposure without unnecessary recovery cost for a beginner."
    ],
    [
      "Fueling",
      "Once long runs approach ~75+ minutes, practice fluids and carbohydrates. Nothing new on race day.",
      "Trains your stomach as well as your legs."
    ],
    [
      "Oman heat",
      "Prefer treadmill, dawn, or late evening. Slow down substantially in heat/humidity and prioritize hydration.",
      "Pace targets become unreliable in hot conditions."
    ],
    [
      "Warning signs",
      "Stop and seek medical assessment for chest pain, fainting, severe dizziness, unusual palpitations, or breathlessness far beyond the effort.",
      "These are not normal training discomforts."
    ],
    [
      "Race goal",
      "Primary goal: complete 21.1 km healthy. A time goal can be added later after 8–12 weeks of consistent running.",
      "Your current limiter is consistency/endurance, not speed."
    ]
  ],
